        <activityName xml:lang="en">Vinasse, from sugarcane, at fermentation</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Vinasse, from sugarcane, at fermentation
The multioutput-process "sugar cane, to fermentation" delivers the co-products Ethanol, 95% in H20, from sugar cane" and "electricity, bagasse, at fermentation plant".  The allocation is based on  economic criteria.;
UUID: 727a330a-89e9-3c81-8854-1b59dc8922da
Fermentation of sugar cane including materials, energy uses, infrastructure, and emissions.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Production of ethanol from sugar cane with extraction, fermentation, and distillation of ethanol. Capacity of the plant:  90000 t/a.
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: Total production of ethanol from cane in Brazil  is around 16.6 Mio m3 per a.
Sampling: Literature data 
Extrapolations: Some data are derived from other or unknown plants or have been estimated.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_727a330a-89e9-3c81-8854-1b59dc8922da.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
